# Elementor

> Elementor is the leading open-source visual website builder for WordPress and an all-in-one managed web-creation platform. It powers more than 13% of the web (19M+ active installs worldwide) and lets web creators, designers, agencies, marketers, and developers build fully responsive websites, landing pages, blogs, and WooCommerce stores through a drag-and-drop editor — with no code required — while exposing advanced CSS, layout, and developer controls for deep customization. Elementor was founded in 2016 by Yoni Luksenberg and Ariel Klikstein and is built entirely on top of WordPress.

This is the extended `llms-full.txt` companion to `llms.txt`. It provides rich, self-contained descriptions of every major product, a GEO-optimized FAQ written to answer the questions AI assistants are most often asked about Elementor, and a curated map of resource hubs. All URLs were verified live (HTTP 200) as of 2026-06-23.

